// Backing up at the very end of the input. The first "ab" is followed by "c", so the scanner walks past the accepting
// state of AB, runs out of transitions and backs up, as in longest-match-backup. The second "ab" is the last two bytes
// of the input, which has no trailing newline: the scanner is still on the accepting state of AB when the input runs
// out, and has to emit AB rather than report the stretch as an error.
//
// The parser is not what this case is about, so the grammar is the single empty production the file format requires.

@scanner {
    AB:   "ab";
    ABCD: "abcd";
}

@parser {
    tokens
        : @empty
        ;
}
